PATCH 636: restore the keyboard callback FAR-CALL operand exchange (board:0030).

Original3446 sets BX=3e0b and ES=CS, then PUSH CS/near CALL46b6.
Actual CS2082 minus main load1119 gives rebased module CS0f69, not
Ghidra's naming segment1000. Helper146b6 exchanges WORD CS:[4f9a]
with AX/ES and WORD CS:[4f98] with BX. These are the operands of the
keyboard ISR's inline FAR-CALL at image14627, hence image14628/1462a;
the old14f98/14f9a aliases overwrite instruction bytes740e8bcb.
Supply the actual segment explicitly and return both old WORDs as a
packed far pointer (old BX offset, old AX/ES segment). Null replacement
still exchanges both words. The two emitted builder tails share actual
3446's asm;3436 is its legacy data-as-code entry, not a second source
initializer. The actual13483 CLC clears the shared carry on builder return.

Reproduce four complete original cases with
python3 -B tools/oracle/capture_callback_exchange.py --output /tmp/wasm-fist-callback-exchange.
The compact source receipt in tools/oracle/callback_exchange_case.json
binds the code/image/binary/scripts and all architecture/16-MiB writes.
Ten source fetches preserve upper GP bits and saved flags for IF0/IF1;
controlled state restoration preserves all39 frames/27518 mixed samples/
end600ms without time adjustment. The port fix accepts WORD pointer data,
explicit caller segment and its existing carry lane only. Original upper
EAX/EBX, raw/lazy flags, far stack, IRQ/IF/instruction time and actual INT9
consumer dispatch remain open; no audio-callback or full-output claim.
